/*
Chains of two to five and/or operators written without parentheses, every
mix of and and or, on six boolean variables (a to f; a chain uses as many as
it needs), each as a value and as an if condition, for all 64 combinations
of true and false (a first: FFFFFF, FFFFFT, ..., TTTTTT). and binds more
tightly than or, and each groups from the left, so a or b and c is
a or (b and c), and a and b or c and d is (a and b) or (c and d). The
expected output was worked out separately from those rules.
*/
class Main
    action Main
        Show("a and b and c", 0)
        Show("a and b or c", 1)
        Show("a or b and c", 2)
